// LspClient.maxon — a Language Server Protocol client for tests: it spawns a real `lsp-server`, speaks
// `Content-Length`-framed JSON-RPC 2.0 over its pipes, and hands each language request back as a typed
// result.
//
// ⭐⭐ **TWO INDEPENDENT AXES, AND CONFLATING THEM IS THE TRAP.**
// - **The RUNNER** — which compiler runs `maxon test tests/lsp` — is BOTH, exactly as
//   `tests/test-command/` is run both ways. A runner broken badly enough to report green having run
//   nothing cannot detect itself, so the bootstrap's `maxon test` is the independent oracle for THE
//   RUNNER.
// - **The SUBJECT** — whose `lsp-server` these tests spawn — is ALWAYS shv2, named by
//   `TestedCompilerStem` below and by nothing else. It does not move with the runner.
//
// ⛔ The bootstrap is a PROTOCOL oracle, never a BEHAVIOUR one: MEASURED 2026-09-02, `bin/maxon
// lsp-server` hangs for ever on stdin EOF and exits 0 where LSP says 1. Point a session at it to settle
// *"what does a correct LSP put in this field"*, never to decide what shv2 must answer.
//
// ⛔⛔ **THE WORKING DIRECTORY IS A CONTRACT, AND IT IS THE CHECKOUT ROOT.** A test binary inherits the
// working directory of the `maxon test` process that launched it, and that command never changes
// directory — so `TestedCompilerStem` is spelled from the root, and a run started anywhere else fails
// LOUDLY in `start()` rather than quietly finding no server.
//
// ⚠ **THREE HAZARDS, ALL THREE REAL, ALL THREE ANSWERED HERE:**
//
// 1. **`release()` OR IT LEAKS.** `StreamingSubprocess` leaks its handle if it is not released and a
//    leak is process exit 101 — which a test reports as a failure of the run, not of an assertion. One
//    client per test, and the client is released before anything is asserted (see the smoke test's
//    shape): an `Expect` that throws must not be able to skip the release.
//
// 2. **A STDERR WRITE CAN DEADLOCK BOTH PROCESSES.** Nothing here drains the server's stderr, and
//    nothing can: stdlib's readers block, this client has no threads, and a blocking drain would simply
//    hang somewhere else. That is SAFE ONLY BECAUSE THE SERVER IS QUIET — `LspServer.failOnBrokenStream`
//    writes ONE line, ONCE, and only on the path that ends the session, which is far below any pipe
//    buffer. It is not an assumption of silence: a server that becomes chatty (or panics with a long
//    stack trace) fills the buffer and both sides then wait on each other for ever. The symptom is a
//    hang that `maxon test`'s shard deadline reports as TIMED OUT, and the cure is a drain in the
//    server's direction, not here.
//    ⚠ **THE SERVER NOW RUNS A WHOLE COMPILE PER `didOpen`, AND EVERY DIAGNOSTIC IT REPORTS WOULD GO TO
//    STDERR.** `LspDiagnostics.publishCheckedDiagnostics` runs it inside a `beginDiagnosticCapture`
//    for exactly this reason. MEASURED 2026-09-03 over a session that opened a document with an error,
//    closed it and shut down: **0 bytes of stderr**.
//
// 3. **A NOTIFICATION CAN ARRIVE BEFORE THE RESPONSE.** MEASURED against the reference server: a
//    `publishDiagnostics` notification does arrive ahead of the first reply — and since shv2 publishes
//    diagnostics too, that is now every request sent after a `didOpen` in this suite. Correlation is
//    therefore STRICT on the integer `id`; a message carrying somebody else's id is dropped, and one
//    carrying no id is STASHED for `awaitPublishedDiagnostics` rather than discarded.
//
// ⛔ No JSON parser and no serializer live here: `stdlib/Json.maxon` is a full RFC 8259 pair, and a
// second one would be this project's signature bug written down again.

// ============================================================================================
// THE SUBJECT
// ============================================================================================

// The server under test, relative to the checkout root, without its host suffix. ONE constant, because
// the SUBJECT axis must not move when the RUNNER does.
let TestedCompilerStem = "maxon-shv2/.maxon/maxon-shv2"

// The subcommand that starts a session. Both compilers spell it the same way, which is what lets these
// tests run under either runner against one server.
let LspServerCommandName = "lsp-server"

// How long the server is given to exit once its stdin is closed or `exit` has been sent. It is well
// under `maxon test`'s 5000 ms shard deadline on purpose: a server that hangs should be reported by this
// client, naming the request, rather than by the harness killing the whole file.
let ServerExitDeadlineMs = 3000

// ============================================================================================
// DOMAIN TYPES
// ============================================================================================

// A zero-based LSP position component — a line, or a character offset within one. ONE alias for both
// because they are one domain: LSP defines each as a zero-based index into the same document, and two
// aliases would be the same bound written down twice.
public typealias LspCoordinate = int(0 to i64.max)

// A document's version as `didChange` carries it. LSP requires it to increase, not to start anywhere in
// particular.
public typealias DocumentVersion = int(0 to i64.max)

// The `tabSize` formatting option. Zero is not a width, so it is not in the domain.
public typealias TabWidth = int(1 to i64.max)

// ⚠ **THE FOUR ALIASES BELOW CARRY THE JSON INTEGER'S OWN RANGE, DELIBERATELY.** Each names a value
// that arrives from the SERVER, and every one of them has a narrower legal range in the specification —
// `SymbolKind` is 1..26, a semantic-token index is bounded by the legend. Narrowing here would turn a
// server sending a value outside its own specification into a range-check PANIC, which reports a crash
// where the truth is a wrong answer this client should hand back for a test to fail on.
public typealias JsonRpcErrorCode = int(i64.min to i64.max)
public typealias SymbolKindCode = int(i64.min to i64.max)
public typealias CompletionKindCode = int(i64.min to i64.max)
public typealias SemanticTokenValue = int(i64.min to i64.max)
public typealias DiagnosticSeverityCode = int(i64.min to i64.max)

// A spawned server's exit status.
public typealias ProcessExitCode = int(i64.min to i64.max)

// The `kind` a server may omit. LSP numbers both `SymbolKind` and `CompletionItemKind` from 1, so 0 is
// outside either enumeration and cannot be mistaken for one of its members.
public let UnspecifiedKind = 0 as SymbolKindCode

public typealias CompletionItemArray = Array with CompletionItem
public typealias TextEditArray = Array with TextEdit
public typealias DocumentSymbolArray = Array with DocumentSymbol
public typealias FoldingRangeArray = Array with FoldingRange
public typealias CodeActionItemArray = Array with CodeActionItem
public typealias LspRangeArray = Array with LspRange
public typealias SemanticTokenValueArray = Array with SemanticTokenValue
public typealias PublishedDiagnosticArray = Array with PublishedDiagnostic

// A span of a document, flat rather than nested. LSP nests it as `{start: {…}, end: {…}}`, but `end` is
// a Maxon keyword and cannot name a field — and the client contract already spells folding ranges and
// code-action ranges flat, so one shape serves every range a test reads.
public type LspRange
	public var startLine as LspCoordinate
	public var startCharacter as LspCoordinate
	public var endLine as LspCoordinate
	public var endCharacter as LspCoordinate

	static function create(startLine LspCoordinate, startCharacter LspCoordinate, endLine LspCoordinate, endCharacter LspCoordinate) returns LspRange
		return Self{startLine: startLine, startCharacter: startCharacter, endLine: endLine, endCharacter: endCharacter}
	end 'create'

	// The span a result carries when it names no location. Only ever read behind an `isPresent` that is
	// false — every result carrying a range says separately whether it has one.
	static function nowhere() returns LspRange
		return Self{startLine: 0, startCharacter: 0, endLine: 0, endCharacter: 0}
	end 'nowhere'
end 'LspRange'

public type TextEdit
	public var range as LspRange
	public var newText as String

	static function create(range LspRange, newText String) returns TextEdit
		return Self{range: range, newText: newText}
	end 'create'
end 'TextEdit'

public type CompletionItem
	public var label as String
	public var kind as CompletionKindCode

	static function create(label String, kind CompletionKindCode) returns CompletionItem
		return Self{label: label, kind: kind}
	end 'create'
end 'CompletionItem'

public type DocumentSymbol
	public var name as String
	public var kind as SymbolKindCode

	static function create(name String, kind SymbolKindCode) returns DocumentSymbol
		return Self{name: name, kind: kind}
	end 'create'
end 'DocumentSymbol'

public type FoldingRange
	public var startLine as LspCoordinate
	public var endLine as LspCoordinate

	static function create(startLine LspCoordinate, endLine LspCoordinate) returns FoldingRange
		return Self{startLine: startLine, endLine: endLine}
	end 'create'
end 'FoldingRange'

public type CodeActionItem
	public var title as String

	static function create(title String) returns CodeActionItem
		return Self{title: title}
	end 'create'
end 'CodeActionItem'

// What the server advertised in its `initialize` response.
//
// ⛔⛔ A capability is a promise, and a server advertises a method capability only when the CLIENT
// declared support for it — so this record is meaningless unless `initialize` sent a realistic
// capability set. MEASURED 2026-09-02 against the reference server: with `capabilities: {}` it
// advertises three members, with a real set it advertises nine. `clientCapabilities` below is what makes
// these fields answerable.
public type InitializeResult
	public var hasTextDocumentSync = false
	public var hasHoverProvider = false
	public var hasCompletionProvider = false
	public var hasDefinitionProvider = false
	public var hasFormattingProvider = false
	public var hasDocumentSymbolProvider = false
	public var hasFoldingRangeProvider = false
	public var hasLinkedEditingRangeProvider = false
	public var hasRenameProvider = false
	public var hasCodeActionProvider = false
	public var hasSemanticTokensProvider = false

	static function create() returns InitializeResult
		return Self{}
	end 'create'
end 'InitializeResult'

// ⭐ **ABSENCE IS `isPresent`, NEVER A SENTINEL.** An empty-string uri meaning "nothing here" is a
// sentinel inside its own domain: it fails silently the day a real result is empty. Both results that
// can be absent say so the same way.
public type HoverResult
	public var isPresent = false
	public var contents as String = ""

	static function nothing() returns HoverResult
		return Self{}
	end 'nothing'

	static function of(contents String) returns HoverResult
		return Self{isPresent: true, contents: contents}
	end 'of'
end 'HoverResult'

public type DefinitionResult
	public var isPresent = false
	public var uri as String = ""
	public var range as LspRange = LspRange.nowhere()

	static function nothing() returns DefinitionResult
		return Self{}
	end 'nothing'

	static function of(uri String, range LspRange) returns DefinitionResult
		return Self{isPresent: true, uri: uri, range: range}
	end 'of'
end 'DefinitionResult'

public type CompletionResult
	public var items as CompletionItemArray

	static function of(items CompletionItemArray) returns CompletionResult
		return Self{items: items}
	end 'of'
end 'CompletionResult'

public type FormattingResult
	public var edits as TextEditArray

	static function of(edits TextEditArray) returns FormattingResult
		return Self{edits: edits}
	end 'of'
end 'FormattingResult'

public type DocumentSymbolsResult
	public var symbols as DocumentSymbolArray

	static function of(symbols DocumentSymbolArray) returns DocumentSymbolsResult
		return Self{symbols: symbols}
	end 'of'
end 'DocumentSymbolsResult'

public type FoldingRangesResult
	public var ranges as FoldingRangeArray

	static function of(ranges FoldingRangeArray) returns FoldingRangesResult
		return Self{ranges: ranges}
	end 'of'
end 'FoldingRangesResult'

public type LinkedEditingRangesResult
	public var ranges as LspRangeArray

	static function of(ranges LspRangeArray) returns LinkedEditingRangesResult
		return Self{ranges: ranges}
	end 'of'
end 'LinkedEditingRangesResult'

public type RenameResult
	public var edits as TextEditArray

	static function of(edits TextEditArray) returns RenameResult
		return Self{edits: edits}
	end 'of'
end 'RenameResult'

public type CodeActionResult
	public var actions as CodeActionItemArray

	static function of(actions CodeActionItemArray) returns CodeActionResult
		return Self{actions: actions}
	end 'of'
end 'CodeActionResult'

public type SemanticTokensResult
	public var data as SemanticTokenValueArray

	static function of(data SemanticTokenValueArray) returns SemanticTokensResult
		return Self{data: data}
	end 'of'
end 'SemanticTokensResult'

// One diagnostic the server PUSHED. It carries every member this client asserts on and no more — the
// range an editor underlines, the severity it colours by, the `E####` code an author greps for, the
// source it groups by, and the sentence it shows.
public type PublishedDiagnostic
	public var range as LspRange
	public var severity as DiagnosticSeverityCode
	public var code as String
	public var source as String
	public var message as String

	static function create(range LspRange, severity DiagnosticSeverityCode, code String, source String, message String) returns PublishedDiagnostic
		return Self{range: range, severity: severity, code: code, source: source, message: message}
	end 'create'
end 'PublishedDiagnostic'

// One `textDocument/publishDiagnostics` notification.
//
// ⭐ **AN EMPTY `items` IS A PUBLISH THAT SAID "NOTHING IS WRONG", AND IT IS NOT THE SAME AS NO PUBLISH
// AT ALL.** The second is what `awaitPublishedDiagnostics` throws on, because a server that stops
// publishing leaves an editor showing whatever it last said.
public type PublishedDiagnostics
	public var uri as String
	public var items as PublishedDiagnosticArray

	static function of(uri String, items PublishedDiagnosticArray) returns PublishedDiagnostics
		return Self{uri: uri, items: items}
	end 'of'
end 'PublishedDiagnostics'

// Whether a stashed publish for the asked-about uri was there to take.
union StashedPublish
	found(published PublishedDiagnostics)
	none
end 'StashedPublish'

// How a session can go wrong in a way that is the SERVER's answer rather than the harness's failure.
//
// ⛔ Nothing that merely prevents a test from running is in here — a missing binary and a failed spawn
// PANIC, because a report that made them read like a wrong answer would send a reader looking for a
// defect in the thing that never ran.
public union LspClientError implements Error
	// The framed stream broke: it ended mid-message, or a read or write failed.
	transportFailed(detail String)
	// A reply arrived that is not the shape LSP defines for the request it answers.
	malformedResponse(detail String)
	// A well-formed JSON-RPC error object. `-32601` is what an unimplemented method answers.
	serverRefused(code JsonRpcErrorCode, message String)
end 'LspClientError'

// ============================================================================================
// THE CLIENT
// ============================================================================================

// A request id. JSON-RPC admits any scalar; this client only ever sends integers, and it starts at 1 so
// that "no request has been sent" is not a value it can produce.
typealias LspRequestIdNumber = int(1 to i64.max)

let FirstRequestId = 1 as LspRequestIdNumber

// A framed body's length in bytes, and how many bytes the line writer appends beyond it.
typealias FrameByteCount = int(0 to i64.max)

// How many messages addressed to somebody else may arrive before this client stops waiting. Server
// notifications are legitimate and unbounded in principle; a budget turns a server that answers nothing
// into a named failure instead of a hang.
typealias SkippedMessageTally = int(0 to i64.max)

let UnaddressedMessageBudget = 64 as SkippedMessageTally

public type LspClient
	var server as StreamingSubprocess
	var nextRequestId as LspRequestIdNumber

	// ⭐⭐ **EVERY SERVER-INITIATED NOTIFICATION THIS CLIENT HAS SEEN AND NOT YET BEEN ASKED FOR, AS RAW
	// FRAME BODIES IN ARRIVAL ORDER.** `awaitReply` used to DISCARD anything not addressed to its
	// request, which was safe only while the server emitted nothing: `publishDiagnostics` arrives ahead
	// of the next reply, so discarding it would make the one message this suite must assert on the one
	// message no test could reach. Held raw and parsed on demand, because most of them are never asked
	// for.
	var notifications as StringArray

	// Spawn this checkout's shv2 `lsp-server` with pipes on all three streams.
	//
	// ⛔ Everything that would stop the session happening at all PANICS rather than throwing: neither a
	// missing binary nor a refused spawn is the server answering wrongly.
	public static function start() returns LspClient
		let binary = testedServerPath()
		if not File.exists(binary) 'noBinary'
			panic("LspClient: the test could not run — there is no compiler at {binary.toString()}. Paths here are relative to the CHECKOUT ROOT, which is the working directory a test binary inherits from `maxon test`; run it from there, and build `{TestedCompilerStem}` first.")
		end 'noBinary'

		var argv = StringArray.create()
		argv.push(LspServerCommandName)

		let spawned = try StreamingSubprocess.spawn(Executable.path(binary), arguments: argv) otherwise (e) 'spawnFailed'
			panic("LspClient: the test could not run — `{TestedCompilerStem} {LspServerCommandName}` did not spawn ({e.displayReason()}).")
		end 'spawnFailed'

		return Self{server: spawned, nextRequestId: FirstRequestId, notifications: StringArray.create()}
	end 'start'

	// End the session and free the OS handle. MUST be called on every path — a dropped
	// `StreamingSubprocess` leaks, and a leak is exit 101.
	//
	// Closing stdin is what lets a server still in its read loop finish; the deadline then force-
	// terminates one that does not, because a survivor holds the pipe and every later spawn in the run
	// inherits a machine with one more orphan on it.
	public function release()
		self.server.closeStdin()
		try self.server.waitWithTimeout(ServerExitDeadlineMs) otherwise ignore
		self.server.release()
	end 'release'

	// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// Lifecycle
	// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

	public function initialize() returns InitializeResult throws LspClientError
		var doc = JsonDoc.create()
		var message = beginMessage(doc, method: MethodInitialize)

		var params = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
		params.putNull(ProcessIdKey)
		params.putNull(RootUriKey)
		params.putNode(CapabilitiesKey, value: clientCapabilities(doc))
		message.putNode(JsonRpcParamsKey, value: params.finish())

		let (replyDoc, result) = try self.sendRequest(doc, message: message)
		let capabilities = try memberNode(replyDoc, of: result, key: CapabilitiesKey)

		var advertised = InitializeResult.create()
		advertised.hasTextDocumentSync = advertises(replyDoc, capabilities: capabilities, key: TextDocumentSyncKey)
		advertised.hasHoverProvider = advertises(replyDoc, capabilities: capabilities, key: HoverProviderKey)
		advertised.hasCompletionProvider = advertises(replyDoc, capabilities: capabilities, key: CompletionProviderKey)
		advertised.hasDefinitionProvider = advertises(replyDoc, capabilities: capabilities, key: DefinitionProviderKey)
		advertised.hasFormattingProvider = advertises(replyDoc, capabilities: capabilities, key: FormattingProviderKey)
		advertised.hasDocumentSymbolProvider = advertises(replyDoc, capabilities: capabilities, key: DocumentSymbolProviderKey)
		advertised.hasFoldingRangeProvider = advertises(replyDoc, capabilities: capabilities, key: FoldingRangeProviderKey)
		advertised.hasLinkedEditingRangeProvider = advertises(replyDoc, capabilities: capabilities, key: LinkedEditingRangeProviderKey)
		advertised.hasRenameProvider = advertises(replyDoc, capabilities: capabilities, key: RenameProviderKey)
		advertised.hasCodeActionProvider = advertises(replyDoc, capabilities: capabilities, key: CodeActionProviderKey)
		advertised.hasSemanticTokensProvider = advertises(replyDoc, capabilities: capabilities, key: SemanticTokensProviderKey)

		return advertised
	end 'initialize'

	public function initialized() throws LspClientError
		var doc = JsonDoc.create()
		var message = beginMessage(doc, method: MethodInitialized)
		message.putNode(JsonRpcParamsKey, value: JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc).finish())
		try self.sendNotification(doc, message: message)
	end 'initialized'

	public function shutdown() throws LspClientError
		var doc = JsonDoc.create()
		// LSP defines `shutdown` as taking no params, and an absent member is not an empty object.
		var message = beginMessage(doc, method: MethodShutdown)
		let (_, _) = try self.sendRequest(doc, message: message)
	end 'shutdown'

	public function exit() throws LspClientError
		var doc = JsonDoc.create()
		try self.sendNotification(doc, message: beginMessage(doc, method: MethodExit))
	end 'exit'

	// Block until the server exits, and report how. A server that never exits is a defect this reports
	// rather than a harness failure, so the deadline throws instead of panicking.
	public function waitForExit() returns ProcessExitCode throws LspClientError
		return try self.server.waitWithTimeout(ServerExitDeadlineMs) otherwise (e) 'neverExited'
			throw LspClientError.transportFailed("the server did not exit within {ServerExitDeadlineMs} ms: {e.displayReason()}")
		end 'neverExited'
	end 'waitForExit'

	// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// Documents — full-text sync (kind 1): every change carries the whole document
	// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

	public function openDocument(uri String, content String) throws LspClientError
		var doc = JsonDoc.create()
		var message = beginMessage(doc, method: MethodDidOpen)

		var item = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
		item.putString(UriKey, value: uri)
		item.putString(LanguageIdKey, value: MaxonLanguageId)
		item.putInt(VersionKey, value: InitialDocumentVersion)
		item.putString(TextKey, value: content)

		var params = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
		params.putNode(TextDocumentKey, value: item.finish())
		message.putNode(JsonRpcParamsKey, value: params.finish())

		try self.sendNotification(doc, message: message)
	end 'openDocument'

	public function changeDocument(uri String, content String, version DocumentVersion) throws LspClientError
		var doc = JsonDoc.create()
		var message = beginMessage(doc, method: MethodDidChange)

		var identifier = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
		identifier.putString(UriKey, value: uri)
		identifier.putInt(VersionKey, value: version)

		var change = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
		change.putString(TextKey, value: content)

		var changes = JsonNodeIdArray.create()
		changes.push(change.finish())

		var params = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
		params.putNode(TextDocumentKey, value: identifier.finish())
		params.putNode(ContentChangesKey, value: doc.add(JsonNode.arrayNode(changes)))
		message.putNode(JsonRpcParamsKey, value: params.finish())

		try self.sendNotification(doc, message: message)
	end 'changeDocument'

	public function closeDocument(uri String) throws LspClientError
		var doc = JsonDoc.create()
		var message = beginMessage(doc, method: MethodDidClose)

		var params = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
		params.putNode(TextDocumentKey, value: textDocumentIdentifier(doc, uri: uri))
		message.putNode(JsonRpcParamsKey, value: params.finish())

		try self.sendNotification(doc, message: message)
	end 'closeDocument'

	// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// Diagnostics — pushed by the server, never asked for
	// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

	// The next `textDocument/publishDiagnostics` for `uri`: taken from the stash if one has already
	// arrived alongside some earlier reply, and otherwise read off the wire.
	//
	// ⭐ **TAKING IS WHAT MAKES A SECOND ASK SEE THE NEXT PUBLISH RATHER THAN THIS ONE AGAIN**, which is
	// the whole of how a `didChange` is observed to REPUBLISH: open, take, change, take, and the two
	// answers are two different notifications rather than one read twice.
	//
	// ⚠ The wait is bounded by the same budget `awaitReply` uses, and for the same reason: a server that
	// never publishes must become a named failure rather than a hang the harness reports as a timeout.
	public function awaitPublishedDiagnostics(uri String) returns PublishedDiagnostics throws LspClientError
		var waited = 0 as SkippedMessageTally

		while waited < UnaddressedMessageBudget 'awaitPublish'
			let stashed = try self.takeStashedPublish(uri)

			match stashed 'arrived'
				found(published) then return published
				none then self.notifications.push(try self.readFrame())
			end 'arrived'

			waited = waited + 1
		end 'awaitPublish'

		throw LspClientError.transportFailed("no textDocument/publishDiagnostics for {uri} arrived within {UnaddressedMessageBudget} messages")
	end 'awaitPublishedDiagnostics'

	// The most recent stashed publish for `uri`, removed from the stash along with every earlier one for
	// the same document. A stale publish left behind would be indistinguishable from a fresh one.
	function takeStashedPublish(uri String) returns StashedPublish throws LspClientError
		var kept = StringArray.create()
		var taken = StashedPublish.none

		for body in self.notifications 'eachStashed'
			let doc = try Json.parse(body) otherwise 'notJson'
				throw LspClientError.malformedResponse("a stashed notification body is not valid JSON: {body}")
			end 'notJson'

			if publishesFor(doc, uri: uri) 'ours'
				taken = StashedPublish.found(try readPublishedDiagnostics(doc, uri: uri))
			end 'ours' else 'somebodyElse'
				kept.push(body.clone())
			end 'somebodyElse'
		end 'eachStashed'

		self.notifications = kept
		return taken
	end 'takeStashedPublish'

	// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// Language features
	// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

	// ⭐ **A METHOD THE SERVER WILL NEVER SERVE, so the refusal it draws is PERMANENT.**
	// The smoke test needs one request that is refused, to prove the client decodes a JSON-RPC error
	// object into `serverRefused` rather than mistaking it for a result. It used to use `hover` for
	// that — which worked only while hover was unimplemented, and went red the day it landed. A test
	// whose subject is "this feature is missing" expires the moment someone does their job.
	// ⇒ The durable subject is the PROTOCOL rule: LSP requires an unknown method to answer
	// `-32601`. This name is reserved for that and is deliberately not an LSP method.
	public function unservedMethodRefusal(uri String) returns HoverResult throws LspClientError
		let (doc, result) = try self.positionRequest(MethodNeverServed, uri: uri, line: DocumentStart, character: DocumentStart)
		if isNull(doc, id: result) 'nothingHere'
			return HoverResult.nothing()
		end 'nothingHere'

		return HoverResult.of(try renderHoverContents(doc, id: try memberNode(doc, of: result, key: ContentsKey)))
	end 'unservedMethodRefusal'

	// ⭐ **IS THIS METHOD SERVED AT ALL?** Sends `methodName` and reports only whether the server answered
	// JSON-RPC's `method not found`. It exists because "served" is a property of the SERVER, not of any one
	// typed method — so asking it ten times through ten typed signatures would be ten chances to ask a
	// slightly different question.
	// ⚠ Position params are sent whatever the method takes. A method that IS served but wants a different
	// shape answers `-32602 invalid params`, which is still an ANSWER: the only thing this reports is the
	// absence of `-32601`.
	public function methodIsServed(methodName String, uri String) returns bool throws LspClientError
		let (_, _) = try self.positionRequest(methodName, uri: uri, line: DocumentStart, character: DocumentStart) otherwise (e) 'refusedOrBroke'
			match e 'reason'
				serverRefused(code, _) then return code != MethodNotFoundCode
				transportFailed or malformedResponse then throw e
			end 'reason'
		end 'refusedOrBroke'

		return true
	end 'methodIsServed'

	public function hover(uri String, line LspCoordinate, character LspCoordinate) returns HoverResult throws LspClientError
		let (doc, result) = try self.positionRequest(MethodHover, uri: uri, line: line, character: character)
		if isNull(doc, id: result) 'nothingHere'
			return HoverResult.nothing()
		end 'nothingHere'

		return HoverResult.of(try renderHoverContents(doc, id: try memberNode(doc, of: result, key: ContentsKey)))
	end 'hover'

	public function definition(uri String, line LspCoordinate, character LspCoordinate) returns DefinitionResult throws LspClientError
		let (doc, result) = try self.positionRequest(MethodDefinition, uri: uri, line: line, character: character)
		return try readDefinition(doc, id: result)
	end 'definition'

	public function completion(uri String, line LspCoordinate, character LspCoordinate) returns CompletionResult throws LspClientError
		let (doc, result) = try self.positionRequest(MethodCompletion, uri: uri, line: line, character: character)
		return try readCompletion(doc, id: result)
	end 'completion'

	// Completion as an editor raises it from a typed character rather than from an explicit invocation.
	// The trigger kind is what tells the server which of the two happened.
	public function completionWithTrigger(uri String, line LspCoordinate, character LspCoordinate, triggerCharacter String) returns CompletionResult throws LspClientError
		var doc = JsonDoc.create()
		var message = beginMessage(doc, method: MethodCompletion)

		var context = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
		context.putInt(TriggerKindKey, value: TriggerCharacterKind)
		context.putString(TriggerCharacterKey, value: triggerCharacter)

		var params = positionParams(doc, uri: uri, line: line, character: character)
		params.putNode(ContextKey, value: context.finish())
		message.putNode(JsonRpcParamsKey, value: params.finish())

		let (replyDoc, result) = try self.sendRequest(doc, message: message)
		return try readCompletion(replyDoc, id: result)
	end 'completionWithTrigger'

	public function formatting(uri String, tabSize TabWidth, insertSpaces bool) returns FormattingResult throws LspClientError
		var doc = JsonDoc.create()
		var message = beginMessage(doc, method: MethodFormatting)

		var options = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
		options.putInt(TabSizeKey, value: tabSize)
		options.putBool(InsertSpacesKey, value: insertSpaces)

		var params = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
		params.putNode(TextDocumentKey, value: textDocumentIdentifier(doc, uri: uri))
		params.putNode(OptionsKey, value: options.finish())
		message.putNode(JsonRpcParamsKey, value: params.finish())

		let (replyDoc, result) = try self.sendRequest(doc, message: message)
		return FormattingResult.of(try readTextEdits(replyDoc, id: result))
	end 'formatting'

	public function documentSymbols(uri String) returns DocumentSymbolsResult throws LspClientError
		let (doc, result) = try self.documentRequest(MethodDocumentSymbol, uri: uri)
		var symbols = DocumentSymbolArray.create()

		for element in try optionalElements(doc, id: result) 'eachSymbol'
			symbols.push(DocumentSymbol.create(try stringMember(doc, of: element, key: NameKey), kind: optionalKind(doc, of: element)))
		end 'eachSymbol'

		return DocumentSymbolsResult.of(symbols)
	end 'documentSymbols'

	public function foldingRange(uri String) returns FoldingRangesResult throws LspClientError
		let (doc, result) = try self.documentRequest(MethodFoldingRange, uri: uri)
		var ranges = FoldingRangeArray.create()

		for element in try optionalElements(doc, id: result) 'eachRange'
			let startLine = try coordinateMember(doc, of: element, key: StartLineKey)
			ranges.push(FoldingRange.create(startLine, endLine: try coordinateMember(doc, of: element, key: EndLineKey)))
		end 'eachRange'

		return FoldingRangesResult.of(ranges)
	end 'foldingRange'

	public function linkedEditingRange(uri String, line LspCoordinate, character LspCoordinate) returns LinkedEditingRangesResult throws LspClientError
		let (doc, result) = try self.positionRequest(MethodLinkedEditingRange, uri: uri, line: line, character: character)
		var ranges = LspRangeArray.create()
		if isNull(doc, id: result) 'nothingHere'
			return LinkedEditingRangesResult.of(ranges)
		end 'nothingHere'

		for element in try elementsOf(doc, id: try memberNode(doc, of: result, key: RangesKey)) 'eachRange'
			ranges.push(try readRange(doc, id: element))
		end 'eachRange'

		return LinkedEditingRangesResult.of(ranges)
	end 'linkedEditingRange'

	public function rename(uri String, line LspCoordinate, character LspCoordinate, newName String) returns RenameResult throws LspClientError
		var doc = JsonDoc.create()
		var message = beginMessage(doc, method: MethodRename)

		var params = positionParams(doc, uri: uri, line: line, character: character)
		params.putString(NewNameKey, value: newName)
		message.putNode(JsonRpcParamsKey, value: params.finish())

		let (replyDoc, result) = try self.sendRequest(doc, message: message)
		return RenameResult.of(try readWorkspaceEdit(replyDoc, id: result, uri: uri))
	end 'rename'

	public function codeAction(uri String, startLine LspCoordinate, startCharacter LspCoordinate, endLine LspCoordinate, endCharacter LspCoordinate) returns CodeActionResult throws LspClientError
		var doc = JsonDoc.create()
		var message = beginMessage(doc, method: MethodCodeAction)

		// The context is required by LSP even when the client knows of no diagnostics at the range.
		var context = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
		context.putNode(DiagnosticsKey, value: doc.add(JsonNode.arrayNode(JsonNodeIdArray.create())))

		var params = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
		params.putNode(TextDocumentKey, value: textDocumentIdentifier(doc, uri: uri))
		params.putNode(RangeKey, value: rangeNode(doc, startLine: startLine, startCharacter: startCharacter, endLine: endLine, endCharacter: endCharacter))
		params.putNode(ContextKey, value: context.finish())
		message.putNode(JsonRpcParamsKey, value: params.finish())

		let (replyDoc, result) = try self.sendRequest(doc, message: message)
		var actions = CodeActionItemArray.create()

		for element in try optionalElements(replyDoc, id: result) 'eachAction'
			actions.push(CodeActionItem.create(try stringMember(replyDoc, of: element, key: TitleKey)))
		end 'eachAction'

		return CodeActionResult.of(actions)
	end 'codeAction'

	public function semanticTokensFull(uri String) returns SemanticTokensResult throws LspClientError
		let (doc, result) = try self.documentRequest(MethodSemanticTokensFull, uri: uri)
		var data = SemanticTokenValueArray.create()
		if isNull(doc, id: result) 'noTokens'
			return SemanticTokensResult.of(data)
		end 'noTokens'

		for element in try elementsOf(doc, id: try memberNode(doc, of: result, key: DataKey)) 'eachValue'
			data.push(try integerAt(doc, id: element))
		end 'eachValue'

		return SemanticTokensResult.of(data)
	end 'semanticTokensFull'

	// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// Request plumbing
	// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

	// The shape every `textDocument/*` request that names a cursor shares.
	function positionRequest(method String, uri String, line LspCoordinate, character LspCoordinate) returns (JsonDoc, JsonNodeId) throws LspClientError
		var doc = JsonDoc.create()
		var message = beginMessage(doc, method: method)
		message.putNode(JsonRpcParamsKey, value: positionParams(doc, uri: uri, line: line, character: character).finish())
		return try self.sendRequest(doc, message: message)
	end 'positionRequest'

	// The shape every request that names only a document shares.
	function documentRequest(method String, uri String) returns (JsonDoc, JsonNodeId) throws LspClientError
		var doc = JsonDoc.create()
		var message = beginMessage(doc, method: method)

		var params = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
		params.putNode(TextDocumentKey, value: textDocumentIdentifier(doc, uri: uri))
		message.putNode(JsonRpcParamsKey, value: params.finish())

		return try self.sendRequest(doc, message: message)
	end 'documentRequest'

	// Address `message` with the next id, send it, and wait for the reply that carries that id back.
	// The reply's document is handed back with the result node because the node is an index into it.
	function sendRequest(doc JsonDoc, message JsonObjectBuilder) returns (JsonDoc, JsonNodeId) throws LspClientError
		let id = self.nextRequestId
		self.nextRequestId = id + 1

		message.putInt(JsonRpcIdKey, value: id)
		doc.root = message.finish()
		try self.writeFrame(Json.stringify(doc))

		return try self.awaitReply(id)
	end 'sendRequest'

	// A notification carries no id, and JSON-RPC forbids answering one — so nothing is read back.
	function sendNotification(doc JsonDoc, message JsonObjectBuilder) throws LspClientError
		doc.root = message.finish()
		try self.writeFrame(Json.stringify(doc))
	end 'sendNotification'

	// ⚠ **THE COUNT INCLUDES THE LINE WRITER'S OWN NEWLINE, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE TRICK.**
	// `writeStdinLine` is stdlib's only stdin writer and it appends an LF. A byte left OUTSIDE the frame
	// would be read by the server as the start of the next message — a header line that is blank and
	// carries no `Content-Length` — which desynchronizes the stream permanently. Counting it instead puts
	// it inside the body, where RFC 8259 allows trailing whitespace after a value, so every conforming
	// JSON parser sees the same message.
	function writeFrame(body String) throws LspClientError
		try self.server.writeStdinLine("Content-Length: {body.byteLength() + LineWriterNewlineByteCount}\r\n\r\n{body}") otherwise (e) 'writeFailed'
			throw LspClientError.transportFailed("writing a {body.byteLength()}-byte message failed: {e.displayReason()}")
		end 'writeFailed'
	end 'writeFrame'

	// Read one framed message: header lines until a blank one, then EXACTLY `Content-Length` bytes.
	//
	// ⛔ The body MUST be taken by count. It carries no terminator, so a line reader blocks for ever on a
	// newline that never arrives, and `readStdoutLineCapped`'s cap is a truncation ceiling rather than a
	// length. `readStdoutBytes` shares the per-handle buffer with the line reader, which is what lets the
	// headers be read by line and the body by count on one stream.
	function readFrame() returns String throws LspClientError
		var contentLength = 0 as FrameByteCount
		var haveContentLength = false
		var inHeaders = true

		while inHeaders 'headers'
			let line = try self.server.readStdoutLine() otherwise (e) 'headerReadFailed'
				throw LspClientError.transportFailed("reading a message header failed: {e.displayReason()}")
			end 'headerReadFailed'

			if line.isEmpty() 'blankLine'
				// EOF reads as an empty line here too, and both end the session: a blank line arriving
				// before a `Content-Length` is not a frame this client can read either way.
				if not haveContentLength 'noFrame'
					throw LspClientError.transportFailed("the server's stdout ended before any Content-Length header")
				end 'noFrame'

				inHeaders = false
			end 'blankLine' else 'headerField'
				let parts = line.split(HeaderFieldSeparator)
				let name = (try parts.get(0) otherwise "").toLower()

				// Every other header is ignored, as the protocol requires of one a peer does not know.
				if name == ContentLengthHeaderName 'contentLengthField'
					let raw = (try parts.get(1) otherwise "").trim()
					contentLength = try int.fromString(raw) otherwise 'notACount'
						throw LspClientError.transportFailed("a Content-Length header is not a byte count: '{raw}'")
					end 'notACount'
					haveContentLength = true
				end 'contentLengthField'
			end 'headerField'
		end 'headers'

		// `readStdoutBytes` cannot throw: a runtime refusal answers "" exactly as a clean EOF does. The
		// short-read check below is therefore the only thing separating a broken stream from a whole frame.
		let body = self.server.readStdoutBytes(contentLength)

		if body.byteLength() != contentLength 'truncated'
			throw LspClientError.transportFailed("the server's stdout ended after {body.byteLength()} of {contentLength} body bytes")
		end 'truncated'

		return body
	end 'readFrame'

	// Read messages until the one addressed to `id` arrives. Anything else — a notification, or a reply
	// to some other request — is skipped, under a budget so that a server answering nothing becomes a
	// named failure rather than a hang.
	function awaitReply(id LspRequestIdNumber) returns (JsonDoc, JsonNodeId) throws LspClientError
		var skipped = 0 as SkippedMessageTally

		while skipped < UnaddressedMessageBudget 'correlate'
			let body = try self.readFrame()
			let doc = try Json.parse(body) otherwise 'notJson'
				throw LspClientError.malformedResponse("a message body is not valid JSON: {body}")
			end 'notJson'

			if addressesRequest(doc, id: id) 'ours'
				return try replyOf(doc)
			end 'ours'

			// A message carrying no id at all is a NOTIFICATION and is kept for whoever asks; one
			// carrying somebody else's id is a reply this client can do nothing with, and is dropped.
			if not hasMember(doc, of: doc.root, key: JsonRpcIdKey) 'aNotification'
				self.notifications.push(body.clone())
			end 'aNotification'

			skipped = skipped + 1
		end 'correlate'

		throw LspClientError.transportFailed("no reply to request {id} arrived within {UnaddressedMessageBudget} messages addressed elsewhere")
	end 'awaitReply'
end 'LspClient'

// The server binary with the suffix this host can actually spawn.
function testedServerPath() returns FilePath
	#if os(Windows)
		let spelled = "{TestedCompilerStem}.exe"
	#else
		let spelled = "{TestedCompilerStem}"
	#endif

	return try FilePath.from(spelled) otherwise panic("LspClient: the test could not run — '{TestedCompilerStem}' is not a spellable path")
end 'testedServerPath'

// ============================================================================================
// BUILDING A MESSAGE
// ============================================================================================

// One JSON object under construction. `JsonNode.objectNode` takes parallel key and child arrays, and
// keeping them in one place is what stops a caller pushing to one and forgetting the other. The document
// travels with the builder because every value added is a node in that arena.
type JsonObjectBuilder
	var doc as JsonDoc
	var keys as StringArray
	var children as JsonNodeIdArray

	static function create(doc JsonDoc) returns JsonObjectBuilder
		return Self{doc: doc, keys: StringArray.create(), children: JsonNodeIdArray.create()}
	end 'create'

	function putString(key String, value String)
		self.keys.push(key)
		self.children.push(self.doc.add(JsonNode.stringNode(value)))
	end 'putString'

	function putInt(key String, value JsonRpcErrorCode)
		self.keys.push(key)
		self.children.push(self.doc.add(JsonNode.numberNode(value)))
	end 'putInt'

	function putBool(key String, value bool)
		self.keys.push(key)
		self.children.push(self.doc.add(JsonNode.boolNode(value)))
	end 'putBool'

	function putNull(key String)
		self.keys.push(key)
		self.children.push(self.doc.add(JsonNode.nullNode()))
	end 'putNull'

	function putNode(key String, value JsonNodeId)
		self.keys.push(key)
		self.children.push(value)
	end 'putNode'

	function finish() returns JsonNodeId
		return self.doc.add(JsonNode.objectNode(self.keys, children: self.children))
	end 'finish'
end 'JsonObjectBuilder'

// The envelope every message shares. The id belongs to requests only, so it is added by the sender.
function beginMessage(doc JsonDoc, method String) returns JsonObjectBuilder
	var message = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
	message.putString(JsonRpcVersionKey, value: JsonRpcVersion)
	message.putString(JsonRpcMethodKey, value: method)
	return message
end 'beginMessage'

function textDocumentIdentifier(doc JsonDoc, uri String) returns JsonNodeId
	var identifier = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
	identifier.putString(UriKey, value: uri)
	return identifier.finish()
end 'textDocumentIdentifier'

function positionNode(doc JsonDoc, line LspCoordinate, character LspCoordinate) returns JsonNodeId
	var position = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
	position.putInt(LineKey, value: line)
	position.putInt(CharacterKey, value: character)
	return position.finish()
end 'positionNode'

function rangeNode(doc JsonDoc, startLine LspCoordinate, startCharacter LspCoordinate, endLine LspCoordinate, endCharacter LspCoordinate) returns JsonNodeId
	var range = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
	range.putNode(StartKey, value: positionNode(doc, line: startLine, character: startCharacter))
	range.putNode(EndKey, value: positionNode(doc, line: endLine, character: endCharacter))
	return range.finish()
end 'rangeNode'

// The params of a `textDocument/*` request that names a cursor, left OPEN so that a caller carrying more
// members — a completion context, a new name — adds them to the same object.
function positionParams(doc JsonDoc, uri String, line LspCoordinate, character LspCoordinate) returns JsonObjectBuilder
	var params = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
	params.putNode(TextDocumentKey, value: textDocumentIdentifier(doc, uri: uri))
	params.putNode(PositionKey, value: positionNode(doc, line: line, character: character))
	return params
end 'positionParams'

// ⛔⛔ **A REALISTIC CAPABILITY SET, NEVER `{}`.** A spec-compliant server advertises a text-document
// capability only when the client declared support for it, so an empty set makes every capability
// assertion fail for a reason that is not a bug. Each feature is declared the same way — the client
// registers statically, not dynamically — which is why the set is one list rather than eleven objects.
function clientCapabilities(doc JsonDoc) returns JsonNodeId
	var textDocument = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)

	for feature in declaredTextDocumentFeatures() 'eachFeature'
		var declaration = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
		declaration.putBool(DynamicRegistrationKey, value: false)
		textDocument.putNode(feature, value: declaration.finish())
	end 'eachFeature'

	var workspace = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
	workspace.putBool(WorkspaceFoldersKey, value: false)

	var capabilities = JsonObjectBuilder.create(doc)
	capabilities.putNode(TextDocumentKey, value: textDocument.finish())
	capabilities.putNode(WorkspaceKey, value: workspace.finish())
	return capabilities.finish()
end 'clientCapabilities'

// Every text-document feature this client supports, spelled as LSP names them under
// `capabilities.textDocument`. `synchronization` is what makes `didOpen` / `didChange` / `didClose`
// legal; the rest are the requests the client exposes.
function declaredTextDocumentFeatures() returns StringArray
	return ["synchronization", "hover", "completion", "definition", "formatting", "documentSymbol", "foldingRange", "linkedEditingRange", "rename", "codeAction", "semanticTokens"]
end 'declaredTextDocumentFeatures'

// ============================================================================================
// READING A REPLY
// ============================================================================================

// Strict correlation on the integer `id`. A notification carries none and a reply to another request
// carries a different one; both are somebody else's message. MEASURED against the reference server: a
// `publishDiagnostics` notification does arrive ahead of the first reply.
function addressesRequest(doc JsonDoc, id LspRequestIdNumber) returns bool
	let idNode = try doc.getChild(doc.root, key: JsonRpcIdKey) otherwise return false
	let node = doc.get(idNode)

	if node.kind != JsonKind.jsonNumber 'notAnIntegerId'
		return false
	end 'notAnIntegerId'

	return trunc(node.numberValue) == id
end 'addressesRequest'

// A JSON-RPC response carries exactly one of `result` and `error`, and WHICH one is the answer.
function replyOf(doc JsonDoc) returns (JsonDoc, JsonNodeId) throws LspClientError
	if hasMember(doc, of: doc.root, key: JsonRpcErrorKey) 'refused'
		let failure = try memberNode(doc, of: doc.root, key: JsonRpcErrorKey)
		let code = try integerMember(doc, of: failure, key: JsonRpcErrorCodeKey)
		throw LspClientError.serverRefused(code, message: try stringMember(doc, of: failure, key: JsonRpcErrorMessageKey))
	end 'refused'

	return (doc, try memberNode(doc, of: doc.root, key: JsonRpcResultKey))
end 'replyOf'

// Whether an object carries `key`. `JsonDoc` answers the lookup only by throwing, and a reply is told
// apart by WHICH member it has — so the presence question is asked of the node's own key list.
function hasMember(doc JsonDoc, of JsonNodeId, key String) returns bool
	let node = doc.get(of)

	for name in node.keys 'eachKey'
		if name == key 'found'
			return true
		end 'found'
	end 'eachKey'

	return false
end 'hasMember'

// A capability is advertised when the server named it and did not answer `false` or `null`. LSP allows
// either a bare `true` or an options object, and both mean the same thing to a client that only asks
// whether the request is worth sending.
function advertises(doc JsonDoc, capabilities JsonNodeId, key String) returns bool
	let declared = try doc.getChild(capabilities, key: key) otherwise return false
	let node = doc.get(declared)

	return match node.kind 'shape'
		jsonNull gives false
		jsonBool gives node.boolValue
		jsonNumber or jsonString or jsonArray or jsonObject gives true
	end 'shape'
end 'advertises'

function isNull(doc JsonDoc, id JsonNodeId) returns bool
	return doc.get(id).kind == JsonKind.jsonNull
end 'isNull'

// `stdlib/Json.maxon`'s access error is private to that file, so a walk here cannot propagate it. These
// four translate it once into the error this client names, which is what lets every reader above use a
// bare `try`.
function memberNode(doc JsonDoc, of JsonNodeId, key String) returns JsonNodeId throws LspClientError
	return try doc.getChild(of, key: key) otherwise 'absent'
		throw LspClientError.malformedResponse("a reply is missing the '{key}' member LSP defines for it")
	end 'absent'
end 'memberNode'

function stringMember(doc JsonDoc, of JsonNodeId, key String) returns String throws LspClientError
	return try doc.getString(of, key: key) otherwise 'notAString'
		throw LspClientError.malformedResponse("a reply's '{key}' member is missing or is not a string")
	end 'notAString'
end 'stringMember'

function integerMember(doc JsonDoc, of JsonNodeId, key String) returns JsonRpcErrorCode throws LspClientError
	return try doc.getInt(of, key: key) otherwise 'notAnInteger'
		throw LspClientError.malformedResponse("a reply's '{key}' member is missing or is not a number")
	end 'notAnInteger'
end 'integerMember'

function integerAt(doc JsonDoc, id JsonNodeId) returns SemanticTokenValue throws LspClientError
	let node = doc.get(id)
	if node.kind != JsonKind.jsonNumber 'notANumber'
		throw LspClientError.malformedResponse("an array this reply must answer with numbers holds something else")
	end 'notANumber'

	return trunc(node.numberValue)
end 'integerAt'

// A position component off the wire. LSP defines these as non-negative, so a negative one is a server
// defect — reported, rather than turned into a range-check panic by an unchecked cast.
function coordinateMember(doc JsonDoc, of JsonNodeId, key String) returns LspCoordinate throws LspClientError
	let value = try integerMember(doc, of: of, key: key)
	if value < 0 'negative'
		throw LspClientError.malformedResponse("a reply's '{key}' is {value}, and LSP positions are zero-based")
	end 'negative'

	return value as LspCoordinate
end 'coordinateMember'

// A `kind` a server may leave out. LSP numbers both enumerations from 1, so the absent value is outside
// either one and cannot be read as a member of it.
function optionalKind(doc JsonDoc, of JsonNodeId) returns SymbolKindCode
	return try doc.getInt(of, key: KindKey) otherwise UnspecifiedKind
end 'optionalKind'

// The elements of a JSON array node.
function elementsOf(doc JsonDoc, id JsonNodeId) returns JsonNodeIdArray throws LspClientError
	let count = try doc.arrayLength(id) otherwise 'notAnArray'
		throw LspClientError.malformedResponse("a member this reply must answer with an array is not one")
	end 'notAnArray'

	var elements = JsonNodeIdArray.create()

	for index in 0 upto count 'eachElement'
		elements.push(try doc.arrayAt(id, index: index) otherwise panic("LspClient.elementsOf: index below the length just measured"))
	end 'eachElement'

	return elements
end 'elementsOf'

// The elements of a result that is an array, or none when the server answered `null`. Several requests
// share exactly this shape: LSP lets each of them return `null` instead of an empty array.
function optionalElements(doc JsonDoc, id JsonNodeId) returns JsonNodeIdArray throws LspClientError
	if isNull(doc, id: id) 'nothingHere'
		return JsonNodeIdArray.create()
	end 'nothingHere'

	return try elementsOf(doc, id: id)
end 'optionalElements'

function readRange(doc JsonDoc, id JsonNodeId) returns LspRange throws LspClientError
	let start = try memberNode(doc, of: id, key: StartKey)
	let finish = try memberNode(doc, of: id, key: EndKey)

	let startLine = try coordinateMember(doc, of: start, key: LineKey)
	let startCharacter = try coordinateMember(doc, of: start, key: CharacterKey)
	let endLine = try coordinateMember(doc, of: finish, key: LineKey)

	return LspRange.create(startLine, startCharacter: startCharacter, endLine: endLine, endCharacter: try coordinateMember(doc, of: finish, key: CharacterKey))
end 'readRange'

// Is this message a `textDocument/publishDiagnostics` naming `uri`? Both halves are asked, because a
// publish for ANOTHER document is a message this client must keep rather than hand back.
function publishesFor(doc JsonDoc, uri String) returns bool
	let method = try doc.getString(doc.root, key: JsonRpcMethodKey) otherwise return false
	if method != MethodPublishDiagnostics 'anotherNotification'
		return false
	end 'anotherNotification'

	let params = try doc.getChild(doc.root, key: JsonRpcParamsKey) otherwise return false
	return (try doc.getString(params, key: UriKey) otherwise "") == uri
end 'publishesFor'

function readPublishedDiagnostics(doc JsonDoc, uri String) returns PublishedDiagnostics throws LspClientError
	let params = try memberNode(doc, of: doc.root, key: JsonRpcParamsKey)
	var items = PublishedDiagnosticArray.create()

	for element in try elementsOf(doc, id: try memberNode(doc, of: params, key: DiagnosticsKey)) 'eachDiagnostic'
		let range = try readRange(doc, id: try memberNode(doc, of: element, key: RangeKey))
		let severity = try integerMember(doc, of: element, key: SeverityKey)
		let code = try stringMember(doc, of: element, key: CodeKey)
		let source = try stringMember(doc, of: element, key: SourceKey)

		items.push(PublishedDiagnostic.create(range, severity: severity, code: code, source: source, message: try stringMember(doc, of: element, key: MessageKey)))
	end 'eachDiagnostic'

	return PublishedDiagnostics.of(uri, items: items)
end 'readPublishedDiagnostics'

function readTextEdits(doc JsonDoc, id JsonNodeId) returns TextEditArray throws LspClientError
	var edits = TextEditArray.create()

	for element in try optionalElements(doc, id: id) 'eachEdit'
		let range = try readRange(doc, id: try memberNode(doc, of: element, key: RangeKey))
		edits.push(TextEdit.create(range, newText: try stringMember(doc, of: element, key: NewTextKey)))
	end 'eachEdit'

	return edits
end 'readTextEdits'

// Hover contents in each of the three shapes LSP admits: a bare string, a `MarkupContent`, and a list of
// either. The list is joined with newlines, which is how an editor stacks the sections it renders.
function renderHoverContents(doc JsonDoc, id JsonNodeId) returns String throws LspClientError
	let node = doc.get(id)

	match node.kind 'shape'
		jsonString then return node.stringValue
		jsonObject then return try stringMember(doc, of: id, key: ValueKey)
		jsonArray then return try renderHoverSections(doc, id: id)
		default throws LspClientError.malformedResponse("a hover reply's contents is neither a string, a MarkupContent nor a list of either")
	end 'shape'
end 'renderHoverContents'

function renderHoverSections(doc JsonDoc, id JsonNodeId) returns String throws LspClientError
	var rendered = ""
	var separator = ""

	for element in try elementsOf(doc, id: id) 'eachSection'
		rendered.append("{separator}{try renderHoverContents(doc, id: element)}")
		separator = HoverSectionSeparator
	end 'eachSection'

	return rendered
end 'renderHoverSections'

// A definition answer in each of the three shapes LSP admits: `null`, one `Location` or `LocationLink`,
// or a list of them. A list answers with its first entry, which is what an editor jumps to.
function readDefinition(doc JsonDoc, id JsonNodeId) returns DefinitionResult throws LspClientError
	if isNull(doc, id: id) 'nothingHere'
		return DefinitionResult.nothing()
	end 'nothingHere'

	if doc.get(id).kind == JsonKind.jsonArray 'aList'
		let candidates = try elementsOf(doc, id: id)
		if candidates.isEmpty() 'noCandidate'
			return DefinitionResult.nothing()
		end 'noCandidate'

		return try readDefinition(doc, id: try candidates.get(0) otherwise panic("LspClient.readDefinition: a non-empty list has a first element"))
	end 'aList'

	// A `LocationLink` names the same two facts under different members.
	if hasMember(doc, of: id, key: TargetUriKey) 'aLink'
		let target = try stringMember(doc, of: id, key: TargetUriKey)
		return DefinitionResult.of(target, range: try readRange(doc, id: try memberNode(doc, of: id, key: TargetRangeKey)))
	end 'aLink'

	let uri = try stringMember(doc, of: id, key: UriKey)
	return DefinitionResult.of(uri, range: try readRange(doc, id: try memberNode(doc, of: id, key: RangeKey)))
end 'readDefinition'

// A completion answer as either a bare list of items or a `CompletionList` wrapping one.
function readCompletion(doc JsonDoc, id JsonNodeId) returns CompletionResult throws LspClientError
	var items = CompletionItemArray.create()
	if isNull(doc, id: id) 'nothingHere'
		return CompletionResult.of(items)
	end 'nothingHere'

	let listed = id if doc.get(id).kind == JsonKind.jsonArray else try memberNode(doc, of: id, key: ItemsKey)

	for element in try elementsOf(doc, id: listed) 'eachItem'
		items.push(CompletionItem.create(try stringMember(doc, of: element, key: LabelKey), kind: optionalKind(doc, of: element)))
	end 'eachItem'

	return CompletionResult.of(items)
end 'readCompletion'

// A `WorkspaceEdit` in either of the two shapes LSP admits, reduced to the edits that apply to `uri` —
// which is the only document a rename test opened.
function readWorkspaceEdit(doc JsonDoc, id JsonNodeId, uri String) returns TextEditArray throws LspClientError
	if isNull(doc, id: id) 'noEdit'
		return TextEditArray.create()
	end 'noEdit'

	if hasMember(doc, of: id, key: ChangesKey) 'byUri'
		let changes = try memberNode(doc, of: id, key: ChangesKey)
		if not hasMember(doc, of: changes, key: uri) 'untouched'
			return TextEditArray.create()
		end 'untouched'

		return try readTextEdits(doc, id: try memberNode(doc, of: changes, key: uri))
	end 'byUri'

	var edits = TextEditArray.create()

	for element in try optionalElements(doc, id: try memberNode(doc, of: id, key: DocumentChangesKey)) 'eachDocument'
		let identifier = try memberNode(doc, of: element, key: TextDocumentKey)
		if (try stringMember(doc, of: identifier, key: UriKey)) != uri 'otherDocument'
			continue
		end 'otherDocument'

		for edit in try readTextEdits(doc, id: try memberNode(doc, of: element, key: EditsKey)) 'eachEdit'
			edits.push(edit)
		end 'eachEdit'
	end 'eachDocument'

	return edits
end 'readWorkspaceEdit'

// ============================================================================================
// WIRE VOCABULARY
// ============================================================================================

let JsonRpcVersion = "2.0"
let JsonRpcVersionKey = "jsonrpc"
let JsonRpcIdKey = "id"
let JsonRpcMethodKey = "method"
let JsonRpcParamsKey = "params"
let JsonRpcResultKey = "result"
let JsonRpcErrorKey = "error"
let JsonRpcErrorCodeKey = "code"
let JsonRpcErrorMessageKey = "message"

let MethodInitialize = "initialize"
let MethodInitialized = "initialized"
let MethodShutdown = "shutdown"
let MethodExit = "exit"
let MethodDidOpen = "textDocument/didOpen"
let MethodDidChange = "textDocument/didChange"
let MethodDidClose = "textDocument/didClose"
let MethodHover = "textDocument/hover"
let MethodDefinition = "textDocument/definition"
let MethodCompletion = "textDocument/completion"
let MethodFormatting = "textDocument/formatting"
let MethodDocumentSymbol = "textDocument/documentSymbol"
let MethodFoldingRange = "textDocument/foldingRange"
let MethodLinkedEditingRange = "textDocument/linkedEditingRange"
let MethodRename = "textDocument/rename"
let MethodCodeAction = "textDocument/codeAction"
let MethodSemanticTokensFull = "textDocument/semanticTokens/full"

// JSON-RPC's reserved code for a method the server does not implement. `methodIsServed` tests for it
// by NUMBER rather than by message text, because the sentence is a server's to word and the code is
// the protocol's.
let MethodNotFoundCode = -32601 as JsonRpcErrorCode

// The probe's position. Any position does — the server refuses the METHOD before it reads the
// params — so this is simply the document's first character.
let DocumentStart = 0 as LspCoordinate

// ⛔ NOT an LSP method, and never to become one. `unservedMethodRefusal` sends it to draw a
// `-32601` that no future implementation can take away. The `maxon/` prefix is the LSP convention
// for a server's own extensions, so it cannot collide with anything the specification adds.
let MethodNeverServed = "maxon/aMethodNoServerServes"

// The one message the SERVER starts. It is a notification, so it carries no id and gets no reply.
let MethodPublishDiagnostics = "textDocument/publishDiagnostics"

let CapabilitiesKey = "capabilities"
let TextDocumentKey = "textDocument"
let WorkspaceKey = "workspace"
let WorkspaceFoldersKey = "workspaceFolders"
let DynamicRegistrationKey = "dynamicRegistration"
let ProcessIdKey = "processId"
let RootUriKey = "rootUri"

let TextDocumentSyncKey = "textDocumentSync"
let HoverProviderKey = "hoverProvider"
let CompletionProviderKey = "completionProvider"
let DefinitionProviderKey = "definitionProvider"
let FormattingProviderKey = "documentFormattingProvider"
let DocumentSymbolProviderKey = "documentSymbolProvider"
let FoldingRangeProviderKey = "foldingRangeProvider"
let LinkedEditingRangeProviderKey = "linkedEditingRangeProvider"
let RenameProviderKey = "renameProvider"
let CodeActionProviderKey = "codeActionProvider"
let SemanticTokensProviderKey = "semanticTokensProvider"

let UriKey = "uri"
let TextKey = "text"
let LanguageIdKey = "languageId"
let VersionKey = "version"
let ContentChangesKey = "contentChanges"
let PositionKey = "position"
let LineKey = "line"
let CharacterKey = "character"
let RangeKey = "range"
let StartKey = "start"
let EndKey = "end"
let ContextKey = "context"
let TriggerKindKey = "triggerKind"
let TriggerCharacterKey = "triggerCharacter"
let OptionsKey = "options"
let TabSizeKey = "tabSize"
let InsertSpacesKey = "insertSpaces"
let NewNameKey = "newName"
let NewTextKey = "newText"
let DiagnosticsKey = "diagnostics"
let SeverityKey = "severity"
let CodeKey = "code"
let SourceKey = "source"
let MessageKey = "message"
let ContentsKey = "contents"
let ValueKey = "value"
let ItemsKey = "items"
let LabelKey = "label"
let KindKey = "kind"
let NameKey = "name"
let TitleKey = "title"
let RangesKey = "ranges"
let DataKey = "data"
let StartLineKey = "startLine"
let EndLineKey = "endLine"
let TargetUriKey = "targetUri"
let TargetRangeKey = "targetRange"
let ChangesKey = "changes"
let DocumentChangesKey = "documentChanges"
let EditsKey = "edits"

// The header field this client reads, lowercased: LSP header names are case-insensitive.
let ContentLengthHeaderName = "content-length"
let HeaderFieldSeparator = ":"

// The one byte `writeStdinLine` appends beyond the body it is given.
let LineWriterNewlineByteCount = 1

// `CompletionTriggerKind.TriggerCharacter` — the client typed a character the server registered.
let TriggerCharacterKind = 2

// The language a `didOpen` announces, and the version a freshly opened document carries.
let MaxonLanguageId = "maxon"
let InitialDocumentVersion = 1 as DocumentVersion

// How hover sections are stacked when a server answers with a list.
let HoverSectionSeparator = "\n"
